 "notes": "Counts and words only. V-leg steps 2 and 3 OWED: no viewer session pair (nothing was minted: a covering and a non-covering viewer cannot be scoped without a hand-typed user-to-advisor link; the ABSENT entries record that no row exists because no address was ever minted). The first 7-shard attempt of Act 4 timed out (shard 0: 300 s, Max Memory 847 MB, nothing written) and two read-only probes (the first 5 clients 11.8 s, the first 25 clients 17.8 s, both 845 MB) showed memory flat from 5 clients, so Amendment 1 re-cut the pass to 28 shards. Dry run, 28 shards: clients 4776, would-write 4012, not available 764, refused 0, peak 846 MB, longest 150 s, the prefix held 18257 objects before and after. The canary (digest dde0e6ed7721) was written once and graded by ~S2 step 1 PASS. Full pass, 28 shards: the sums equal the dry run's; the prefix gained 4011 (4012 minus the canary); peak 838 MB, longest 150 s. After: 4012 filled objects; series, summary and other counts equal to before. Largest event by memory: 846 MB (a dry-run shard); longest: 150 s. The page has not been looked at. A viewer covering a client can now read that client's filled report through the live route. The 'other' count is every key that is not a client summary, a filled report or a series object, i.e. the 6954 manifests (the series objects, also 6954, are counted by series_prefixes); counting the series objects in it as well gives 13908 before and after, equal either way."
